Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||11-10-2001||08:03 PM||||Thought I would show these.  Some people haven't seen a Fiero's Guts before.  This is a first time for me as well, and I'm the surgeon.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB100026.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB100030.JPG"> <P>There's still a lot to go, but it's come a long way since I bought it 3 weeks ago.  I paid $500 for it, all I wanted was the doors (Power windows and locks), the Factory sunroof, and the seats with the speakers in the headrests (which will of course be reupholstered with MR. Mikes).  So far I've sold most of the interior stuff and the headlight motors and have made all of my money back.  Still have all the body panels and all of the electrical stuff if anybody is interested.  This makes me feel kind of sad though, knowing that once this was a beautiful new fiero on the road that somebody had neglected and let it's condition hit the crapper.  Proof that Fiero's can rust out (sorry).<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PB100027.JPG"> <BR>Even under the Rocker Panels was nothing but rust that fell apart when the rockers where removed.  Behind the quarter panels as well, and most of what was behind the rear clip as well.  Poor Thing.||||reg||1
Z||000001||gt boy||11-10-2001||08:48 PM||||wow...and i thought the gt that i just parted out wast rusty!!<P>..i did sell the whole chassis totally stripped with a blown motor and a good 4spd to a fella for 100.00...so don't send it to the wreckers yet....remember "one mans trash is another mans treasure".||||reg||1
